# Product Updates

Keeping your products up to date is an important part of maintaining quality and customer satisfaction on the Codexeron Marketplace.

This guide explains how product updates are managed.

---

# Overview

Product updates allow sellers to:

- Fix bugs
- Improve performance
- Add new features
- Improve security
- Maintain compatibility
- Update documentation

Regular updates help keep products reliable and valuable for customers.

---

# Before Updating

Before publishing an update:

- Test all changes.
- Update the documentation.
- Update the changelog.
- Verify the version number.
- Ensure the product remains functional.

---

# Version Number

Every update must include a new version number.

Recommended versioning:

```
v1.0.0
v1.0.1
v1.0.2
v1.1.0
v2.0.0
```

Use Semantic Versioning whenever possible.

---

# Changelog

Every update should include a changelog.

Example:

```
v1.1.0

Added:
- New reporting module

Improved:
- Dashboard performance

Fixed:
- Login validation issue
```

---

# Updating Product Files

When submitting an update:

- Upload the latest product files.
- Remove unnecessary files.
- Include updated documentation.
- Verify installation instructions.

Only upload files required for the current version.

---

# Review Process

Product updates may be reviewed before they become available.

Review helps ensure:

- Product quality
- Security
- Compatibility
- Marketplace compliance

Additional information may be requested during the review process.

---

# Breaking Changes

If an update introduces breaking changes:

- Clearly explain the changes.
- Update the documentation.
- Inform users of any required actions.
- Increase the version number appropriately.

---

# Security Updates

Security-related updates should be submitted as soon as possible.

If a critical vulnerability is discovered:

- Fix the issue immediately.
- Submit an updated version.
- Update the changelog.
- Provide a brief description of the security improvement.

---

# Best Practices

To provide a better experience:

- Release updates regularly.
- Maintain backward compatibility whenever possible.
- Keep documentation current.
- Test before every release.
- Use meaningful version numbers.

